manifest.json lists every head file in this folder so the app can resolve
case mismatches between iRealPro song titles (e.g. "You And The Night And
The Music") and on-disk filenames (e.g. "You and the Night and the Music").
GitHub Pages doesn't return directory listings, so without this file the
PWA on Android can't see what's available.

Regenerate after adding/removing/renaming a song file. From this folder:

    ls | grep -iE '\.(musicxml|mid)$' | python -c "import sys, json; print(json.dumps(sorted([line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]), indent=2))" > manifest.json

Or any equivalent command that produces a JSON array of filenames.
